---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../config/site.config";
// Source: spec/reviewcatcher-legal-pages.md ("Complaints Procedure" section).
// Strong draft — for solicitor review before final use; not legal advice.
---

<Layout title={`Complaints | ${siteConfig.name}`} description={`How to raise a complaint with ${siteConfig.name}.`}>
  <main class="page-shell">
    <h1>Complaints Procedure</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated: {siteConfig.legal.pagesLastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>We want to hear if something's not right, and we aim to fix it quickly.</p>

      <h2>How to raise a complaint</h2>
      <p>
        Contact us at <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contact.email}`}>{siteConfig.contact.email}</a>
        {siteConfig.contact.phone && <> or {siteConfig.contact.phone}</>} with the details. Please
        tell us what happened and what outcome you're looking for.
      </p>

      <h2>What happens next</h2>
      <p>
        We'll acknowledge your complaint within 2 working days and aim to give you a full
        response within 10 working days. If we need longer, we'll tell you why and when to expect
        an answer.
      </p>

      <h2>Data protection complaints</h2>
      <p>
        If your complaint is about how we've handled personal data and you're not satisfied with
        our response, you have the right to complain to the Data Protection Commission — the
        Irish supervisory authority — at <strong>dataprotection.ie</strong> or 21 Fitzwilliam
        Square South, Dublin 2, D02 RD28.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
